<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.1//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml11/DTD/xhtml11.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:ext="http://exslt.org/common"><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
<title>IRS_IDR0 | Jon's Arm Reference</title><meta name="description" content="IRS Identification Register 0. Contains read-only fields with information about the IRS GIC component."></meta><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"></meta><link rel="stylesheet" href="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.css"></link><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/static/normalize.css"></link><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/static/main.css"></link></head><body><p class="discontinuation-notice" data-pagefind-ignore="all"><b>PER ARM'S REQUEST, THIS SITE WILL BE DISCONTINUED ON 4 DECEMBER 2026. :(</b><br></br>

      Arm's lawyers have notified me to take down this site or face legal action. <br></br>

      To all of the fans of this site over the years (even the ones at Arm): thank you for your support! I'm glad I could provide a resource so many people found value in. I will look into solutions that can potentially keep bookmarks and links working. <br></br>

      — Jon
    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">IRS_IDR0</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">IRS Identification Register 0</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>IRS Identification Register 0. Contains read-only fields with information about the IRS GIC component.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_GICv5_EXT is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to IRS_IDR0 are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p><h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>IRS_IDR0 is a 32-bit register.</p>
      <p>This  register is part of the <a href="irs_config_frame.html">IRS_CONFIG_FRAME</a> block.</p><h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_16">IRSID</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-15_15">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-14_14">INTCFG</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-13_13">MPAM2</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-12_12">SWE</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-11_11">MPAM</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-10_10-1">MEC</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-9_9-1">SETLPI</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-8_8">VIRT_ONE_N</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-7_7">ONE_N</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-6_6">VIRT</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="4"><a href="#fieldset_0-5_2">PA_RANGE</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-1_0">INT_DOM</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_16">IRSID, bits [31:16]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Unique identifier for this IRS in the system.</p>
    
      <p>This value is the same across all Interrupt Domains for this IRS.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-15_15">Bit [15]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-14_14">INTCFG, bit [14]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>IRS register for interrupt configuration support.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>INTCFG</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>The IRS interrupt configuration register interface is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>The IRS interrupt configuration register interface is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-13_13">MPAM2, bit [13]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Memory Partitioning And Monitoring (MPAM) 2 support.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>MPAM2</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>MPAMv2.0 is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>MPAMv2.0 is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table><p>Support for MPAMv2.0 is optional.</p>
<p>If MPAMv2.0 is supported, MPAMv1.x is not supported.</p></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-12_12">SWE, bit [12]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Software error reporting support in the Interrupt Domain.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>SWE</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>Software error reporting is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>Software error reporting is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table>
      <p>Support for Software error reporting is optional.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-11_11">MPAM, bit [11]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Memory Partitioning And Monitoring (MPAM) 1.x support.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>MPAM</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>MPAMv1.x is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>MPAMv1.x is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table><p>Support for MPAMv1.x is optional.</p>
<p>If MPAMv1.x is supported, MPAMv2.0 is not supported.</p></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-10_10-1">MEC, bit [10] <span class="condition">when IRS_IDR0.INT_DOM == '11'</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Support for Memory Encryption Contexts (MEC) for the Realm Interrupt Domain.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>MEC</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>Memory Encryption Contexts are not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>Memory Encryption Contexts are supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table>
      <p>Support for MEC is optional.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-10_10-2"> <span class="condition">Otherwise</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-9_9-1">SETLPI, bit [9] <span class="condition">when IRS_IDR2.LPI == '1'</span>:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Whether the IRS implements the IRS SETLPI register.</p>
<p>The IRS SETLPI register allows an MSI to set a physical LPI Pending without translation by an ITS.</p><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>SETLPI</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>The IRS does not implement the IRS SETLPI register.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>The IRS implements the IRS SETLPI register.</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-9_9-2"> <span class="condition">Otherwise</span>:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-8_8">VIRT_ONE_N, bit [8]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Whether virtual 1ofN is supported.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>VIRT_ONE_N</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>Virtual 1ofN is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>Virtual 1ofN is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table><p>This field is <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>, if any of the following are true:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Virt is 0.</p>

</li><li>
<p>ONE_N is 0.</p>

</li></ul></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-7_7">ONE_N, bit [7]:
      </h4><div class="field"><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>ONE_N</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>1ofN is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>1ofN is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-6_6">VIRT, bit [6]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>This field is <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span> for the EL3 Interrupt Domain</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>VIRT</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>Virtualization is not supported.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>Virtualization is supported.</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-5_2">PA_RANGE, bits [5:2]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Physical Address range supported.</p>
<p>The physical address range corresponds to the system physical address size.</p>
<p>The value of this field is the same for all Interrupt Domains across all IRSs in the system.</p><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>PA_RANGE</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0000</td><td>
          <p>32 bits, 4GB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0001</td><td>
          <p>36 bits, 64GB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0010</td><td>
          <p>40 bits, 1TB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0011</td><td>
          <p>42 bits, 4TB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0100</td><td>
          <p>44 bits, 16TB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0101</td><td>
          <p>48 bits, 256TB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0110</td><td>
          <p>52 bits, 4PB</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0111</td><td>
          <p>56 bits, 64PB</p>
        </td></tr></table>
      <p>All other values are reserved.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-1_0">INT_DOM, bits [1:0]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>The Interrupt Domain that the register frame containing this register controls.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>INT_DOM</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b00</td><td>
          <p>Secure</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b01</td><td>
          <p>Non-secure</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b10</td><td>
          <p>EL3</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b11</td><td>
          <p>Realm</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><div class="access_mechanisms"><h2>Access Instructions</h2><p>Accesses to this register use the following encodings:</p><div class="access_block"><p>Accessible at offset <span class="hexnumber">0x0000</span> from IRS_CONFIG_FRAME</p></div><p>Accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RO</span>.</p><p style="text-align: right">
      ()
      </p></div><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
